              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Im a Utah girl, so I'm very picky about my fry sauce! I made it with half ketchup half bbq sauce and it turned out wonderful. Thanks for the recipe!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "msouleusa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this sauce and on the first go around I did not care for it. Then I had an idea, instead of mayo I used ranch dressing, diced up a couple of slices of jalapeno, mixed it up and put it in the frig over night. Tried it the next morning, GREAT (like tony the tiger says).",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-16T05:37:53.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marcy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is just so easy and fast to make, and has a great taste! I don't use onion powder because it's usually so high in sodium, so I used garlic powder instead, plus low-fat mayonnaise and no-salt ketchup. My version is healthier (low-fat, low-sodium) than the original recipe but probably just as good!",
            "datePublished": "2008-02-25T16:43:27.823Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Abbey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is pretty good, it doesn't have a lot of taste but it's a good addition to my home made potato wedges. I mixed in some extra cayenne for more kick.",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-13T20:05:05.907Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mrhozer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yep, add half bbq sauice and half ketchup to really make it pop! Try a splash of dill pickle juice or red wine vinegar and it really brings the flavors to life. Excellent recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2010-03-23T14:08:37.720Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JChester"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making a much simpler version of this for years. I use about 1/2 &amp; 1/2 mayo and ketchup. Then I add Dijon mustard, by taste, 'til I get the extra 'zip' I want. Sometimes I'll add a little chili powder. This way it doesn't need cayenne, salt or pepper. But... I may try adding onion powder next time.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-24T21:21:58.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Molly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This sauce worked well as a dip for our fries and for our sandwich. It was served with 'Waffle Sandwich with Cheese, Spinach and Spicy Mustard' and 'Yummy Cheese Fries' both from AR and a tossed salad. I did up the cayenne to 1/4 tsp. and next time I would increase it just a little more. We tend to like spicy. Thanks Cindy, for sharing your version of Fry Sauce. I had never heard of Fry Sauce until AR. We enjoyed it.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-19T19:18:02.860Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jenne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Followed reviewers suggestions and added barbeque sauce. Also added a little chopped onion. Ate with fries and chicken nuggets, the flavor came out even more with the nuggets. Will be making this a lot!! Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-23T14:12:13.517Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marnie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made the version with 1/2 ketchup and 1/2 bbq sauce, and added some dried chilies for a bit of kick. Great with sweet potato fries!",
            "datePublished": "2016-08-09T01:28:44.020Z"
          },
          {
